<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n97084" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στραγγός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ή</span>,
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">όν</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>twisted, crooked</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Phot.
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Suid.
			</span></i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>complicated, irregular</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πυρετοί</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ruf.
				</span></i>
			 ap. <i><span class="en">
				Orib.
				8.24.30
			</span></i>: 
				Comp.
			, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">αἱ μονοπάθειαι τῶν ὀφθαλμῶν
				-ότεραί εἰσιν</span>
			<i>more violent</i> or <i>serious</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Cass.
				<u>Pr.</u>
				14
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>shameless</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Phot.
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Suid.
			</span></i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στράγξ</span>) <i>flowing drop by drop</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κάθαρσις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Sor.
					1.2
				</span></i>
			, al.: 
				Comp.
			, <i><span class="en">
				Antyll.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Orib.
				8.6.6
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Sor.
				1.27
			</span></i>. Adv.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-γῶς, καθαίρεσθαι</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				31
			</span></i>.—In <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Phot.
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Suid.
			</span></i> written <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στραγός</span>; in cod. <i><span class="en">
				Sor.
			</span></i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στραγκός</span>: 
				Comp.
			
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στραγώτερος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Antyll.
				</span></i>
			 ap. Orib.l.c., <i><span class="en">
				Phot.
			</span></i> (
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ότερος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Suid.
				</span></i>
			).</div>
